bg3le Noesis: clear a MultiBindingExpression's destroyed tree element before it is called through

On top of 0001-0007. Two crashes at client UnloadLevel (claude-run-2 S024 07:37, the Act 1 ->
Shadow-Cursed Lands transition; 2026-10-10 10:40:53, a load_game reload) are the same use-after-free,
now fully symbolized from 0007's crash log and the core (bg3 has a .symtab):

  MultiBindingExpression::GetSourceValue+0x4a  call *0x3c8(%rax), rax = a heap free-list word
  <- MultiBindingExpression::Evaluate <- PropertyListener::OnPropertyChanged <- ... <-
  BindingExpression::OnDataContextChanged <- ContentControl::OnPropertyChanged <-
  ItemContainerGenerator::RemoveAll <- ItemCollection::SetView <- ... <- BaseCollection::Clear

The game clears a view-model collection during the unload; a container's DataContext change makes a
MultiBinding re-evaluate. The expression (alive) belongs to a NoesisApp::InvokeCommandAction (refcount 1)
owned by TriggerActionCollection <- EventTrigger <- StyleTriggerCollection <- Setter (behaviors applied
through a Style). Its +0xb0 is the target's tree element, a raw pointer cached once by the constructor
(FindTreeElement); that element was destroyed normally (refcount 0, DependencyObject base vtable left at
+0x10, free-list word at +0). Its two readers, GetSourceValue and BeforeSet, already handle null.

Now a dead tree element (refcount 0, or a vtable whose first slot is not code of a loaded object) is
cleared before either runs: GetSourceValue through its 2 direct call sites (hook_call_sites), BeforeSet
through its MultiBindingExpression vtable slot (8). Both are refused unless the `mov 0xb0(%reg),%rdi`
bytes are where this build has them. Logs the first 5 and every 100th; BG3LE_GUARD_BINDINGS=0 disables.

Against bg3le 3728a68 (v0.3.6) with 0001-0007. Applied by tools/build_bg3le.sh.
